   "text": "I read the molecule as a disulfide-cyclised peptide with a lipidated, PEG-linked N-terminal side chain, and wrote the SMILES residue by residue.\n\n**Macrocycle (N\u2192C direction):** Pen(B) \u2192 Asn \u2192 Thr \u2192 7-methyl-Trp \u2192 Lys(Ac) \u2192 Pen(A). The two penicillamine side chains are joined by an S\u2013S bond.\n\n**N-terminal branch on Pen(B):**\n- The Pen(B) amine is acylated by a D-Lys. That Lys has an N-terminal acetyl on its \u03b1-amine.\n- Its \u03b5-amine carries two 8-amino-3,6-dioxaoctanoyl (PEG-type) units in a row.\n- These are followed by \u03b3-Glu, whose \u03b1-NH is acylated by a decanedioic (sebacic) acid.\n- I counted the diacid chain as 8 CH\u2082 groups between the two carbonyls. The zigzag in the image was hard to count, so this length is the least certain part of the reading.\n\n**C-terminal chain from Pen(A) (N\u2192C):**\n- Tyr(O-CH\u2082CH\u2082NH\u2082)\n- 2-naphthylalanine\n- 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid\n- Lys(Ac)\n- Asn\n- 3-pyridylalanine\n- N-methylglycinamide\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- I worked out R/S from the wedges and hashes for both Pen centres, the Asn in the ring, the Tyr(OCH\u2082CH\u2082NH\u2082) and the linker Lys. Both Pen centres come out R, i.e. L-Pen. The ring Asn and the Tyr derivative are S (L). The linker Lys is R, i.e. D-Lys.\n- For the remaining residues I did not check the drawn wedges and assumed the L configuration. The two I am least sure of are the 2-naphthylalanine and the \u03b3-Glu.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)CCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C"
